Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D231471", "files": ["dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cb8de6f0deb138c8cc41d6252931d96014ebdd66", "parents": ["64544b16dbbbe44147534a836831e234469df97a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1928512 - Use opaque backstop color for page canvas background. r=dholbert, a=RyanVM\n\nThis restores behavior from before bug 1835864, effectively.\n\nThe top level image document's root element has transparent background.\nBefore that patch, we used to blend that with\nGetDefaultBackgroundColorDraw(), which was white.\n\nThis should generally not change behavior, because the page frame itself\nis white, but it does on PrintTargetWindows (probably a cairo bug?),\nwhere it causes our page content clip not to apply.\n\nIn any case, restoring behavior here is trivial, so let's do that for\nnow, I'll file a follow-up bug for the underlying issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D228514", "files": ["layout/generic/nsPageContentFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-page/pseudo-first-margin-004-print.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8436cfcddff30096c839217df5f6a5875c5ac73d", "parents": ["cb8de6f0deb138c8cc41d6252931d96014ebdd66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1934919 [Linux] Set drop timeout back to 1 sec to avoid long freezes r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D230961", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsDragService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "879c538efbde1f3befefaea6dc9afdc38d02f431", "parents": ["8436cfcddff30096c839217df5f6a5875c5ac73d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1920998 - Try to work around macOS panel positioning bug. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D230129", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/popup.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8729ceb8a558dd1fe2e4a4c9df405f1b2f2cd379", "parents": ["879c538efbde1f3befefaea6dc9afdc38d02f431"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734114724, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "332": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 8729ceb8a558 (bug 1920998) for browser_ext_popup_select.js permafails.", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/popup.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ee62573c0019f5baf8ab3c420a4888cff708681a", "parents": ["8729ceb8a558dd1fe2e4a4c9df405f1b2f2cd379"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zach Hoffman \u003czach@zrhoffman.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1926164 - Negate in_negation when nesting r=dshin,jwatt a=RyanVM\n\n`in_negation` was `true` in cases where it should be `false`, like\n`:not(:not(...))`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D226582", "files": ["servo/components/selectors/context.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-always-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-always-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-always-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-always-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-always-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-always-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-always-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-always-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-never-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-never-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-never-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-is-never-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-never-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-never-matches-negated-first-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-never-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/negated-never-matches-negated-last-of-type-when-ancestor-changes.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2ef9c3c6109942b3061bc7a98b4dfa739c16be76", "parents": ["ee62573c0019f5baf8ab3c420a4888cff708681a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734138083, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "333": {"changesets": [{"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1916193 - stop always allowing opening the Windows Store,  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220810\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232125", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "38b1579734e224bc72cddd532877d3b864d7d910", "parents": ["2ef9c3c6109942b3061bc7a98b4dfa739c16be76"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734138396, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "334": {"changesets": [{"author": "David P \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1926196: Use HashSet for wifi listeners  a=pascalc\n\nThis avoids invalidating iterators when mutating the collection during iteration.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D230422\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232096", "files": ["netwerk/wifi/nsWifiMonitor.cpp", "netwerk/wifi/nsWifiMonitor.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f9207caf1bbb3f2d79378f429fc5e7667d76ff54", "parents": ["38b1579734e224bc72cddd532877d3b864d7d910"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David P \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1926196: Iterate over a copy of WifiListenerData to allow mutation  a=pascalc\n\nTo avoid iterators being invalidated during iteration, this needs a collection\nthat allows mutation during iteration (like std::set) or a copy. This uses\na copy to get the best asymptotic performance.\n\nIncludes a test that both OnChange and OnError allow listener removal.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D231002\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232097", "files": ["netwerk/wifi/gtest/TestWifiMonitorListenerRemoval.cpp", "netwerk/wifi/gtest/moz.build", "netwerk/wifi/nsWifiMonitor.cpp", "netwerk/wifi/nsWifiMonitor.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aa34db7b015a9157f143dafabdacfd5fe8e59fa5", "parents": ["f9207caf1bbb3f2d79378f429fc5e7667d76ff54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David P \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1935354: Define STDMETHODCALLTYPE in TestWifiMonitorListenerRemoval for MinGW  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D231304\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232098", "files": ["netwerk/wifi/gtest/TestWifiMonitorListenerRemoval.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8d99d7daa333cb78c1dca63873a4d69aea9a1fa6", "parents": ["aa34db7b015a9157f143dafabdacfd5fe8e59fa5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734376954, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "335": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1890155: If we can't get an HWND when clients call IAccessible2::windowHandle, fall back to the first top level Gecko HWND we can find.  a=RyanVM\n\nThis hack is needed to avoid a crash in the Microsoft IA2 -\u003e UIA proxy.\nSee the code comments for details.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D230189\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232307", "files": ["accessible/windows/ia2/ia2Accessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b5166d40089e05058ad3dcf2ce325a8d9b86f16f", "parents": ["8d99d7daa333cb78c1dca63873a4d69aea9a1fa6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734402912, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "336": {"changesets": [{"author": "Filipe La\u00edns \u003clains@riseup.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1935621 - Fix virtual environment sysconfig path calculation r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden a=pascalc\n\nSigned-off-by: Filipe La\u00edns \u003clains@riseup.net\u003e\n\nSigned-off-by: Filipe La\u00edns \u003clains@riseup.net\u003e\n\nSigned-off-by: Filipe La\u00edns \u003clains@riseup.net\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D231480", "files": ["python/mach/mach/site.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e270c9ac0dbb6ef54f66e7691a5ed922ee504ffd", "parents": ["b5166d40089e05058ad3dcf2ce325a8d9b86f16f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734447265, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "337": {"changesets": [{"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914742 [Linux] Don't use gtk_targets_include_uri() to check URI types r=emilio a=RyanVM", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsDragService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "27c5e4229000a40d4de12c0ee9eb83aabca64e66", "parents": ["e270c9ac0dbb6ef54f66e7691a5ed922ee504ffd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1913643 [Linux] Drag&Drop check received data r=emilio a=RyanVM", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsDragService.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsDragService.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e14f7a15583018e6b127162582cbe148aa9d2003", "parents": ["27c5e4229000a40d4de12c0ee9eb83aabca64e66"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734456965, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "338": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr128 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes -  a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232388", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/addons-mlbf.bin", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/addons-mlbf.bin.meta.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/translations-models.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/translations-wasm.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c1585616dbd2c97c0dfda203512c1bf22d6483e2", "parents": ["e14f7a15583018e6b127162582cbe148aa9d2003"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1886423 - Update search config tests.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D205208\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232248", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/searchconfigs/test_ecosia.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "80804a4f2b2df8460c9fca53a294ff945df9eeec", "parents": ["c1585616dbd2c97c0dfda203512c1bf22d6483e2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1734457153, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "339": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1924363 - Eagerly resolve sum nodes during parsing  a=RyanVM\n\nProduct nodes are eagerly resolved during parse time, but sum nodes are\nnot. This might cause floating point inprecision in sum nodes, which\nleads to invalid calculations, e.g. `round(down, (7 - 1) / 3, 1)` would\nend up being `round(down, (2.3333333 - 0.33333334), 1)`, then\n`round(down, 1.99999996, 1)`, which equals `1`, which is incorrect.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225936\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232498", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/generics/calc.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/calc.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/round-function.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4f008c71b12e001ae54b7fcd4787b266764c28bf", "parents": ["80804a4f2b2df8460c9fca53a294ff945df9eeec"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_128_6_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_128_6_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1734535868, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}}
}";